Preamble

Sanctuary is a sovereign health infrastructure platform created by and for Trans, gender-expansive, and LGBTQ+ communities in Baltimore, Maryland. It was built in direct response to the documented threat that commercial cloud-based electronic health record systems pose to community members whose gender identity, transition history, and health records can be weaponized against them by hostile legal actors, government agencies, and institutions operating in bad faith.

The purpose of this license is to ensure that Sanctuary remains free, community-controlled, and structurally incapable of being turned against the communities it was built to protect. It does this by combining the access and collaboration principles of copyleft open source licensing with explicit, enforceable ethical use restrictions that reflect the specific threat model of Trans and LGBTQ+ communities in the current political environment.

This license is grounded in the belief that software infrastructure is not neutral. A platform designed to protect Trans health records can only fulfill that purpose if its legal terms prohibit uses that would undermine that protection. Freedom to use and modify Sanctuary is therefore conditioned on a commitment not to weaponize it — not against the communities it serves, not in service of surveillance, discrimination, or state-sponsored harm, and not for private profit extracted from community need.

The copyright holder, Aziza Okoro of ThriveBMore / Radiant Threshold Staffing Solutions, grants the rights described in this license in service of that purpose. Recipients of this license are invited to build on Sanctuary, improve it, deploy it, and share it — within a framework that keeps it permanently in community hands.

  Section 1

  Definitions

For the purposes of this License, the following terms have the meanings set forth below.

"Software"  The Sanctuary sovereign health infrastructure platform, version 5.0, including all source code, compiled code, configuration files, documentation, templates, training materials, and associated files distributed under this License.

"Licensor"  Aziza Okoro, operating as ThriveBMore and/or Radiant Threshold Staffing Solutions, Baltimore, Maryland — the original copyright holder of the Software.

"Licensee"  Any individual, organization, or entity that receives, uses, copies, modifies, or distributes the Software under the terms of this License.

"Derivative Work"  Any work that incorporates, is based upon, is derived from, or substantially modifies the Software or any portion thereof, whether in source code, compiled, or any other form.

"Community Organization"  A nonprofit organization, mutual aid collective, fiscal-sponsored project, community health center, peer support program, harm reduction program, housing advocacy organization, legal aid organization, or similar entity whose primary mission is the direct service of Trans, gender-expansive, LGBTQ+, or other marginalized communities.

"Commercial Use"  Any use of the Software or a Derivative Work in which a person or entity charges money, collects fees, accepts payment, generates revenue, or derives financial benefit directly from the Software or its capabilities — including but not limited to subscription services, software-as-a-service deployments, consulting arrangements where the Software is a deliverable, and any sale or licensing of the Software or Derivative Works.

"Protected Communities"  Trans people, gender-expansive people, nonbinary people, intersex people, lesbian, gay, bisexual, and queer people, people living with HIV, people with substance use disorders, people experiencing housing instability, immigrants, people of color, and any other communities that have been historically targeted by discriminatory legal, law enforcement, governmental, or institutional action.

"Weaponization"  Any use of the Software or a Derivative Work to collect, store, transmit, analyze, report, or otherwise process information in ways that expose, surveil, discriminate against, cause legal jeopardy for, or otherwise harm members of Protected Communities or the organizations that serve them.

"Source Code"  The human-readable form of the Software, including all HTML, CSS, JavaScript, configuration files, and documentation in their original editable form.

"Network Deployment"  Operating the Software or a Derivative Work as a service accessible to users over a network, including the internet or any private network, regardless of whether end users can access the underlying Source Code.

