The exercise of any right granted in Section 2 is conditioned on the following requirements, which apply to all Licensees.

3.1  Copyleft — Share Alike

Any Derivative Work distributed or deployed must be made available under the terms of this License and no other. You may not apply additional restrictions, different license terms, or proprietary terms to a Derivative Work. The freedom to use, study, modify, and share Sanctuary must be preserved in every downstream version of the Software.

If you operate a Derivative Work as a Network Deployment — that is, if you run a modified version of Sanctuary as a service that other people or organizations access — you must make the complete Source Code of your deployed version available to all users of that service upon request, at no charge. This requirement applies even if you have not formally distributed the Derivative Work. Running a modified version for others to use is itself a form of distribution under this License.

3.2  Attribution

All copies, Derivative Works, and Network Deployments must include the following attribution in a location that is reasonably prominent and accessible to users:

