You may not remove, obscure, or modify any existing copyright notices, license notices, or attribution statements present in the Software. You may add your own attribution notices for your modifications, provided they do not conflict with or undermine the original attribution required above.

3.3  License Transmission

Every time you distribute the Software or a Derivative Work, the recipient automatically receives a license from the Licensor to use, copy, modify, and distribute the Software under the terms of this License. You may not impose any additional restrictions on the recipients' exercise of those rights. You are not responsible for enforcing compliance by third parties, but you may not facilitate or enable violations of this License.

3.4  Integrity of the Source Code

You may distribute the Software in modified form only if you also distribute the Source Code under this License, and only if the modified version bears a clear notice stating that it is a modification of the original Sanctuary Software, the date of modification, and the identity of the modifying party. Modifications must not misrepresent the origin of the Software or imply endorsement by the Licensor of the modified version.

  Section 4

  Prohibited Uses

This Section contains absolute prohibitions. There are no exceptions to the restrictions in Section 4, regardless of purpose, context, or any other license terms. These restrictions apply to all Licensees, including Community Organizations, governments, researchers, and individuals.

4.1  Prohibition on Weaponization

No Licensee may use the Software, any Derivative Work, or any component thereof in any manner that constitutes Weaponization as defined in Section 1. This prohibition includes but is not limited to:

(a)  Using the Software to collect, aggregate, store, or transmit data about members of Protected Communities in ways that expose them to legal jeopardy, immigration enforcement, law enforcement action, or discrimination.

(b)  Using the Software to generate, compile, or transmit reports, lists, or records of individuals based on gender identity, sexual orientation, HIV status, substance use history, or other Protected Community characteristics, for use by law enforcement, government agencies, or hostile third parties.

(c)  Using the Software to build or operate any surveillance system targeting members of Protected Communities or the organizations that serve them.

(d)  Modifying the Software to remove, disable, or circumvent any privacy protection, encryption function, data sovereignty feature, or security control.

(e)  Using the Software in any manner that would, directly or indirectly, assist in prosecuting, persecuting, harming, exposing, or discriminating against members of Protected Communities in connection with gender-affirming care, sexual orientation, or gender identity.

4.2  Prohibition on Commercial Use

No Licensee may engage in Commercial Use of the Software or any Derivative Work without a separate, written Commercial License Agreement executed by the Licensor. Commercial Use without such an agreement is a material breach of this License and immediately terminates all rights granted herein.

For the avoidance of doubt, the following are not considered Commercial Use under this License:

(a)  A Community Organization deploying Sanctuary to manage client records in service of its mission, even if that organization receives grant funding, government contracts, or Medicaid reimbursement for services.

(b)  A staff member or contractor being paid by a Community Organization to maintain, configure, or deploy Sanctuary as part of their employment duties, where the Software itself is not the product being sold.

(c)  An organization receiving a fee for training services related to Sanctuary deployment, provided the Software itself is provided free of charge.

4.3  Prohibition on Use by Hostile Actors

The Software may not be used by, on behalf of, or in service of any of the following:

(a)  Any government agency, law enforcement body, immigration enforcement agency, or intelligence agency whose activities include the targeting, surveillance, prosecution, or deportation of members of Protected Communities based on gender identity, sexual orientation, HIV status, or substance use history.

(b)  Any organization that has, within the five years preceding use, advocated for, funded, lobbied for, or implemented policies that restrict access to gender-affirming care, criminalize LGBTQ+ identity, or remove legal protections from Trans or LGBTQ+ individuals.

(c)  Any organization or individual that is actively engaged in litigation against Trans or LGBTQ+ individuals or organizations on the basis of gender identity or sexual orientation.

(d)  Any political party, campaign, political action committee, or advocacy organization whose stated or demonstrated platform includes opposition to Trans rights, LGBTQ+ nondiscrimination protections, or gender-affirming care.

4.4  Prohibition on Proprietary Enclosure

No Licensee may use patent claims, digital rights management, contractual restrictions, technical measures, or any other mechanism to prevent recipients of the Software or Derivative Works from exercising the rights granted to them under this License. You may not use the Software as a component in a proprietary system in a manner that effectively denies recipients access to the Source Code or restricts their rights under this License.

  Section 5

  Commercial Licensing

Organizations or individuals seeking to engage in Commercial Use of Sanctuary must obtain a separate written Commercial License Agreement from the Licensor. The Licensor retains sole discretion over whether to grant commercial licenses, to whom, and on what terms.

Any Commercial License granted by the Licensor must, at minimum, require the commercial Licensee to:

(a)  Maintain all prohibitions in Section 4 of this License in the commercial deployment.

(b)  Contribute a portion of revenue derived from the Software to a fund supporting free deployment of Sanctuary at Community Organizations, at a rate and structure negotiated with the Licensor.

(c)  Provide a mechanism for Community Organizations to access equivalent functionality at no cost.

(d)  Submit to periodic review by the Licensor to confirm ongoing compliance with the terms of the Commercial License.

Inquiries regarding commercial licensing should be directed to the Licensor at: aziza@sanctuary-health.org. The Licensor is under no obligation to respond to or grant commercial license requests.

  Section 6

  Enforcement and Termination

6.1.  Automatic Termination. Any violation of Section 3 (Conditions of Use), Section 4 (Prohibited Uses), or Section 5 (Commercial Licensing) automatically and immediately terminates all rights granted under this License to the violating Licensee, without notice or action required from the Licensor. Termination of rights under this License does not affect the rights of any other Licensee who has received the Software and remains in compliance.

6.2.  Cure Period for Technical Violations. For violations of Section 3 only (Conditions of Use), a Licensee whose rights have been automatically terminated may have those rights reinstated if the violation is cured within thirty (30) days of the Licensee first becoming aware of it. No cure period applies to violations of Section 4 (Prohibited Uses). Weaponization, commercial use without a license, and use by prohibited actors cannot be cured retroactively.

6.3.  Right to Enforce. The Licensor reserves the right to seek all available legal remedies for violations of this License, including injunctive relief, damages, and attorney's fees, to the fullest extent permitted by applicable law.

6.4.  Community Reporting. Any person or organization that becomes aware of a use of Sanctuary that may violate Section 4 is encouraged to report it to the Licensor at aziza@sanctuary-health.org. The Licensor will investigate reported violations and may take enforcement action at its discretion.

6.5.  Survival. Sections 1, 4, 6, 7, 8, and 9 of this License survive any termination.

